>>9) Level of Buildings - This is easy, just let the makelevel code
>>   create a dungon level and then convert the solid rock and corredor
>>   types to unlit room. This will yield a level with buildings with
>>   doors. The only thing to watch out for are the teleport traps
>>   for vaults. And be sure to leave a boundry of solid rock around
>>   the whole level.

Good idea.  I think one area Nethack should work on his having some 
variety in the levels.  Nethack is better in this regard than Hack,
but I think more variety (especially at the low cost in extra coding
that this would require) is a good idea.

Now we get into Ari's suggestions, which are saved from earlier postings
and are (in my opinion) much less interesting.

>Shopping mall

A bad idea except at Level 0, ie., for outfitting a blank character,
which is the character generation method I prefer.

>Wand of animation

Mostly silly, and open for abuse, but not a bad idea.

>Parrot - a new pet

I think a host of new pets is in order.

>Potion of oil

I don't see that this adds much, especially if implemented as liquid
dynamite, which most people (Ari included) seem to think it is.
Medieval oil was more like vegatable oil, folks.  It's hardly likely
to explode, or even burn.

>Earplugs

This doesn't add anything, just another ) item to ignore.

>Cage - a kind of box

Why?

